As I said, it can be done, but it is not tidy the way that {da, de, di} is 
(though, of course, these have to go to subscripts eventually as well) -- nor 
nearly as clear, either to the eye or the understanding.  I'm not sure what 
the ideal solution would be (I personally like taking {ce'u} as lambda and 
using the regular variables) or even a practical one, but if we are going to 
do much more of this lambdaing, we need somthing, just to make usuable 
example.

